    "note": "**Ruler — characters genuinely tight now. You were right; my \"geometry floor\" was wrong.**\n\nThe gap wasn't a hard limit — it was that the glyph font was capped by the cell size, and the glyph BAND was short. The fix uses the geometry you pointed at:\n\n- **Glyph band now takes ~80% of the strip's height** (was ~54%), so the font can grow tall.\n- **Font cap raised to 1.6× the cell width.** A glyph's ink is ~0.55× its font, so at this size the ink is ~0.9× the cell — it nearly fills the cell and the neighbours sit almost touching, while still fitting inside the cell horizontally (no clip).\n\nNet on this seed: glyph font ~45px → **~69px**, inter-character gap ~23px → **~10px (≈55% closer)**. Strip is still **full-width**, glyphs are still **depth-1 sibling cells** (no per-glyph overlay stack), so there's **no overlay-depth / tofu risk** even on long strings.\n\nIf you want them literally overlapping (ink past the cell edge), that needs per-glyph absolute layers — which tofus past ~25 chars — so I kept it at \"nearly touching,\" which is robust for every layout. Say the word if you want the overlapping variant for short strings only.\n\n*(172 tests green. Only the fixed/short-string strip changed; the long-string paged path is untouched.)*",
    "question": "Are the characters tight enough now (~55% closer, nearly touching, full-width)? If yes I think the teaching is done — back to the stress batch (10 layouts already staged in stress/) to find where it struggles.",
